1. heydamir/unslop, https://github.com/heydamir/unslop
   Copyright Damir Sokolovsky. Licensed under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0), https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
   Used: the idea of a nine-step fix order and several checklist items (short text without trailing full stops, restrained font weights, icon consistency, 4 px spacing rhythm, nested radius, one primary action, "change amount" verdict, a final "does it still look like a template" look).
   Changes: all text and code here are newly written; the checks are implemented as measurable rules and fixtures. This is an adaptation and is not endorsed by the original author. The name "unslop" belongs to its author.

2. Leonxlnx/taste-skill, https://github.com/Leonxlnx/taste-skill
   MIT License. Copyright (c) 2026 Leonxlnx
   Used: rule ideas for page-frame issues, app screens, visual poverty and accessibility (see docs/SOURCES.md).

3. Emil Kowalski's skills (emilkowalski/skills)
   MIT License. Copyright (c) 2026 Emil Kowalski
   Used: general motion ranges (press, reveal and dialog durations; easing guidance), re-stated as starting points.

4. NiazMorshed2007/reanimate, https://github.com/NiazMorshed2007/reanimate
   MIT License. Copyright (c) NiazMorshed2007 (copyright year not verified by this project).
   Used: the method of measuring a reference animation as numbers (same conditions, spec table, compare timing and not pixels). No code taken.

5. pbakaus/impeccable, https://github.com/pbakaus/impeccable
   Apache License 2.0. Copyright Paul Bakaus.
   Used: inspiration for naming recurring AI patterns (side stripes, skipped heading levels, small touch targets). No code or text taken.

6. Google design.md specification (section order Overview, Colors, Typography, Layout, Elevation, Shapes, Components, Do/Don't). Used as a layout convention for the DESIGN.md template; this project adds a Motion section.

